  "verbalization": "Caruifolin C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Thrombopoietin, which is involved in the regulation of blood cell production. This target is engaged by multiple compounds, including Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine and Bungeiside A, which both direct their activity to HepG2, a human liver cancer cell line. The evidence suggests that Caruifolin C may act through a similar mechanism, potentially by modulating Thrombopoietin activity, which could influence cellular processes in HepG2 cells. The consistent involvement of Thrombopoietin as a target across different compounds implies a common pathway or mechanism of action, although the specific molecular details remain unclear. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Caruifolin C may interact with HepG2 through a Thrombopoietin-dependent mechanism, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
